# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# TypeScript project-reference build stamps, written by `tsc -b`
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Large source screen recordings (transcoded outputs live in public/)
*.mov

# Thesis source material: reference only, never shipped. Kept out of the repo
# because it is 48MB, and because the presentation bundles a hydro animation
# downloaded from YouTube — fine in a talk, not ours to publish.
/animations/

# Node bundle for the build-time render (scripts/prerender.mjs); never deployed
dist-ssr

# Screenshots dropped in the repo root by a browser-driving script. Fourteen
# megabytes of them were committed once; they belong in a scratch directory.
/*.png
/*.jpg

# The mascot pipeline's own inputs and outputs, kept on disk and out of the
# repo. Only two things here are load-bearing and both stay tracked: the drawing
# the pipeline reads (mascot/mascot_refined/athena-source-1254.png) and the
# eight webp plates it ends up producing (src/assets/athena-agent*.webp), which
# are what the site actually ships.
#
# Everything else was 34MB of a repo that Amplify clones on every build: the
# candidate drawings from two rounds of generation, superseded by the one that
# was chosen; the outputs of an older pipeline run under mascot/out, whose
# filenames no longer match what plates.py writes; and tools/mascot/out-*.png,
# which is 17MB of intermediate 2508px plate that `python3 pipeline.py` puts
# back in one command. See tools/mascot/README.md.
/mascot/image_*
/mascot/mascot_refined/image_*
/mascot/out/
/tools/mascot/out-*.png
